6th regnal This records the allotment (by the temple authorities) out of the dēvadāna land year. at Tiruvalandurainallūr, of 1 1/4 kalañju of gold, 3 ka'am of paddy and a pair of cloths, as remuneration to a śakkai of Aḍalaiyūr for enacting 3 parts of a śakkai-kūttu (dance-dramas?) in the temple on the day of a festival occurring in Aśvini asterism in
Aippigai month. This śakkai-kūttu is mentioned in other inscriptions also (vide M.E.R.
for 1915, Part II, para. 22).Read more (1 KB)
